1
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:50,000
The first independent film to have successfully
licensed original Beatles recordings.

2
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Good Ol' Freda is a music, documentary, history film directed by Ryan White.

3
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:18,000
The story of Freda Kelly, a shy Liverpudlian teenager asked to work for
a young local band hoping to make it big: The Beatles.

4
00:22:56,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Their loyal secretary from beginning to end, Freda tells
her tales for the first time in 50 years.

5
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Self, played by Freda Kelly.

6
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Self, played by Tony Barrow.

7
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:14,000
Self, played by Billy Hatton.

8
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:58,000
Self, played by Ringo Starr.

9
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:42,000
Self (archive footage), played by John Lennon.

10
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
Self (archive footage), played by Paul McCartney.

11
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:10,000
Freda Kelly (born 14 July 1945) is an Irish secretary who was employed by the Beatles and their manager,
Brian Epstein, from 1962 until 1972 and was secretary of the group's official fan club.

12
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:54,000
Kelly worked with the band as they rose from local popularity to
world-wide fame and through their dissolution.

13
01:14:32,000 --> 01:14:38,000
A 2013 documentary, Good Ol' Freda, chronicled Kelly's ten-plus
year association with the group and its members.

14
01:20:16,000 --> 01:20:22,000
The film explores themes of musical, secretary, rock band.
